\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Oft in danger, Oft In woe,
\par Onward, Christians, onward go;
\par Fight the fight, maintain the strife,
\par Strengthened with the Bread of Life.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Shrink not, Christians: will ye yield?
\par Will ye quit the painful field?
\par Will ye flee in danger's hour?
\par Know ye not your Captain's power?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Let your drooping hearts be glad;
\par March in heavenly armour clad:
\par Fight, nor think the battle long;
\par Soon shall victory tune your song.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Let not sorrow dim your eye,
\par Soon shall every tear be dry;
\par Let not fears your course impede,
\par Great your strength if great your need.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Onward then to glory move,
\par More than conquerorr ye shall prove;
\par Though opposed by many a foe,
\par Christians soldiers, onward go.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

